WEBVTT

00:02.202 --> 00:03.669
Legend has it that...

00:04.838 --> 00:07.636
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons...

00:07.974 --> 00:13.310
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.781 --> 00:19.946
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.066 --> 00:40.495
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.774 --> 00:46.610
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.148 --> 00:54.053
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.722 --> 00:59.488
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.592 --> 01:02.789
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.566 --> 01:13.631
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:13.807 --> 01:19.643
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:20.513 --> 01:27.783
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:27.954 --> 01:36.362
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:37.063 --> 01:38.724
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.475 --> 01:51.911
<i>Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

02:05.058 --> 02:06.047
Ryoma!

02:07.360 --> 02:09.021
You've got to hang on! Ryoma!

02:09.529 --> 02:10.518
Ryoma!

02:15.402 --> 02:16.960
Izumi...

02:18.805 --> 02:19.999
Ryoma...

02:22.308 --> 02:30.408
It looks like I won't be
able to keep my promise...

02:33.753 --> 02:37.621
Can you forgive me?

02:39.993 --> 02:45.590
Still, the fact that I got to meet you...

02:46.666 --> 02:52.161
...that alone made me happy.

02:54.407 --> 02:55.601
Ryoma!

02:59.045 --> 03:00.444
Why...

03:00.847 --> 03:05.250
Why didn't you draw your sword?

03:08.221 --> 03:09.848
Until the very end...

03:11.157 --> 03:16.094
Until the very end, you were just...

03:19.332 --> 03:21.664
...too gentle for your own good!

03:23.937 --> 03:25.495
Izumi...

03:27.173 --> 03:32.076
Do you think it was the
Shinsengumi after all?

03:37.217 --> 03:38.878
Hijikata!

03:42.021 --> 03:47.516
<i>Farewell, My Friend</i>

03:52.632 --> 03:55.066
<i>Shinsengumi Headquarters</i>

04:00.773 --> 04:01.865
Halt!

04:22.896 --> 04:24.557
Who the hell are you?

04:24.831 --> 04:27.857
Are you aware that you've broken
into the Shinsengumi headquarters?

04:31.804 --> 04:32.600
Deputy Commander!

04:32.739 --> 04:33.933
Calm yourself down!

04:40.046 --> 04:41.877
Is he challenging us?

04:46.853 --> 04:49.185
He's here!

04:57.497 --> 04:59.522
You tell Hijikata for me...

05:00.033 --> 05:02.593
...that Izumi Mutsu has arrived.

05:23.523 --> 05:27.584
You've broken into the
Shinsengumi Headquarters alone...

05:28.795 --> 05:33.664
Moreover, you're striding
through our property as if...

05:33.800 --> 05:37.065
...no one was here to challenge you...

05:37.370 --> 05:39.065
Deputy Commander!

05:40.907 --> 05:42.534
Izumi Mutsu...

05:43.042 --> 05:46.136
So we meet for the first time
since the Teradaya Incident!

05:48.681 --> 05:50.774
Hijikata!

05:51.884 --> 05:53.476
I warned you before...

05:53.820 --> 05:57.722
If I ever catch you laying
a hand on a friend of mine...

05:59.058 --> 06:02.186
...then I'll smash your Shinsengumi
to pieces with my own two hands!

06:05.698 --> 06:07.222
What are you talking about?

06:11.337 --> 06:12.497
Don't tell me...

06:12.639 --> 06:15.199
Surely you're not saying that
Sakamoto's been assassinated?

06:15.375 --> 06:17.104
Drop the clueless act!

06:29.522 --> 06:31.683
So it is true, after all...

06:31.858 --> 06:35.350
...but the Shinsengumi
had nothing to do with it.

06:53.913 --> 06:55.642
I have come here today to warn you...

06:56.282 --> 07:00.343
...whatever you do, be on your
guard against the Shinsengumi...

07:05.024 --> 07:06.889
Sorry to bother you.

07:10.229 --> 07:11.526
Hijikata...

07:12.598 --> 07:15.123
I'm sure you know a
man by the name of Ito...

07:15.301 --> 07:16.165
Yes.

07:16.769 --> 07:18.634
He's a traitor.

07:19.038 --> 07:22.940
As soon as he saw that a new era
was upon us, he abandoned our group.

07:23.176 --> 07:26.168
Now he's the leader of a group trying
to ally itself with the Tobaku faction.

07:27.947 --> 07:28.971
Don't touch him.

07:29.649 --> 07:30.741
What?

07:31.484 --> 07:32.974
I said don't touch him!

07:35.421 --> 07:38.857
That man is mine to kill.

07:43.329 --> 07:46.196
If anyone's going to avenge
Ryoma Sakamoto's death...

07:46.399 --> 07:47.559
...it will be me!

07:51.204 --> 07:52.728
I see what you're saying.

07:52.872 --> 07:55.534
That's just the kind
of plot Ito would hatch.

07:55.908 --> 07:58.274
Sakamoto's murder is
the gift he'll offer...

07:58.411 --> 08:02.040
...to Satsuma and Choshu as he
rushes into their arms, huh?

08:02.882 --> 08:07.285
It's not the Shogunate who wanted
Sakamoto out of the way, you see...

08:08.054 --> 08:09.749
It was Satsuma and Choshu's
anti-Bakufu aggression...

08:09.822 --> 08:11.119
...that was being suppressed.

08:11.357 --> 08:16.920
Framing the Shinsengumi for the
crime but making off with the spoils...

08:19.665 --> 08:22.498
Don't you dare get in my way, Hijikata!

08:33.813 --> 08:35.110
Okita?

08:35.348 --> 08:37.976
You have attacked the
Shinsengumi headquarters.

08:38.084 --> 08:40.882
You're not going to slip away
without answering for that!

08:42.088 --> 08:43.749
Soushi, back off!

08:44.390 --> 08:47.257
Forgive me, Hijikata.

08:47.627 --> 08:50.892
Please, just humor
me this one last time.

08:56.068 --> 08:59.003
I feel very lucky to have met you.

08:59.405 --> 09:03.307
I didn't perfect my skills all these
years just so I could kill others...

09:04.377 --> 09:07.778
I've reached the point where
I can believe that of myself.

09:08.981 --> 09:11.381
Step aside, Okita.

09:11.784 --> 09:14.378
If you get in my way, I'll kill you.

09:16.189 --> 09:17.622
I won't step aside.

09:18.591 --> 09:19.489
Soushi!

09:19.892 --> 09:23.089
Fortunately, you're
ready to go for the kill.

09:23.596 --> 09:26.497
Enough to compel even a member
of the Band of Assassins...

09:26.632 --> 09:28.964
...the Shinsengumi, to
yield the road to you.

09:31.270 --> 09:35.331
I want to challenge you
as just a swordsman, and...

09:35.842 --> 09:38.436
...not as Soushi Okita
of the Shinsengumi.

09:45.518 --> 09:49.887
Genius, that's what they call it...

09:50.623 --> 09:52.784
...that's what you are.

09:56.262 --> 09:59.823
All the same, don't just
throw your life away!

10:02.468 --> 10:04.060
So you're going to flee?

10:06.339 --> 10:09.274
It's your chest, isn't it?
That's what's ailing you...

10:09.375 --> 10:11.309
How did you know?

10:12.578 --> 10:14.944
My eyes are not mere knotholes!

10:15.848 --> 10:17.645
Make a full recovery first.

10:18.251 --> 10:21.846
It would give me no joy to
defeat you as you are now.

10:22.922 --> 10:26.323
When you've recovered,
then I'll take you on.

10:26.659 --> 10:29.423
Mutsu, is that a promise?

10:29.896 --> 10:32.126
When that day comes, then
you'll really fight me?

10:32.565 --> 10:33.691
Yes.

10:34.433 --> 10:38.164
I'm a man who's never broken
any promise he's made...

10:42.074 --> 10:43.974
...except for one.

10:52.118 --> 10:52.982
Soushi...

10:53.786 --> 10:55.378
Hijikata-san...

10:56.322 --> 11:00.315
A mysterious man, isn't he?

11:00.860 --> 11:01.952
Yes.

11:02.895 --> 11:04.920
Did you see him, Kondoh?

11:05.398 --> 11:08.424
That's Mutsu, the one I've
been telling you about.

11:09.135 --> 11:13.196
You're right. He's a mysterious fellow.

11:13.539 --> 11:15.973
And he's to be feared.

11:16.909 --> 11:21.175
If it had actually been the
Shinsengumi that murdered Sakamoto...

11:21.914 --> 11:24.508
...could you have beaten him, Toshizo?

11:25.518 --> 11:27.145
Who knows?

11:27.386 --> 11:29.411
I know my entire body
feels ready to fight, but...

11:32.658 --> 11:38.528
The blood of the Cold-hearted
Demon Killer is on fire, eh?

12:08.294 --> 12:10.524
Mutsu, what are you doing?

12:10.930 --> 12:13.262
Where can I find that damned Ito?

12:15.034 --> 12:16.467
Aburano...

12:16.736 --> 12:24.006
I've heard that he sometimes dines
at a restaurant in Aburanokoji...

12:35.521 --> 12:38.388
Really, my dear Ito, you
are as brilliant as they say!

12:38.591 --> 12:40.115
Yes, truly brilliant!

12:40.359 --> 12:45.023
Still, do you really think
Saigou will accept our terms?

12:45.264 --> 12:46.993
No need for concern.

12:47.466 --> 12:51.994
Since Sakamoto was more or less the
greatest hero of the Restoration...

12:52.405 --> 12:54.999
...Satsuma would never accept
us if they found out that...

12:55.107 --> 12:57.598
...we were responsible for his death...

12:58.010 --> 13:01.878
...but I've already reached an
understanding with Hanjiro Nakamura.

13:02.515 --> 13:06.975
Indeed, Nakamura insisted
on killing Sakamoto himself...

13:08.954 --> 13:12.788
...but as it turned out, Hanjiro
never made it to Oomiya...

13:16.429 --> 13:19.057
Who the hell are you?

13:20.700 --> 13:23.032
Are you with the Shinsengumi?

13:25.337 --> 13:29.171
I'm a friend of Ryoma Sakamoto!

13:30.810 --> 13:32.004
You bastard!

13:44.123 --> 13:45.147
Ito!

13:45.357 --> 13:46.949
He's powerful...

13:48.561 --> 13:49.926
...but still...

13:50.996 --> 13:55.490
I see, you're the reason why Hanjiro
the Assassin never made it to Oomiya.

13:55.634 --> 13:56.396
However...

13:56.902 --> 13:58.529
...don't forget, now!

13:59.872 --> 14:06.334
I'm the man who struck Sakamoto down
before he could even draw his sword!

14:07.947 --> 14:09.812
You have no chance against me
unarmed.

14:25.564 --> 14:26.895
You're quick.

14:27.333 --> 14:28.391
But...

14:29.368 --> 14:33.327
His back is to the wall,
that will be his downfall!

14:37.443 --> 14:38.034
Huh?

14:40.146 --> 14:41.135
That's ridiculous!

14:41.280 --> 14:44.943
He advanced without dodging? But how
could he have beaten my sword?

14:48.854 --> 14:49.912
Too slow.

14:50.289 --> 14:51.756
You're way too slow!

14:52.158 --> 14:55.127
Ryoma Sakamoto was a lot
faster with his sword!

14:57.663 --> 15:00.723
It wasn't that Ryoma
couldn't draw his sword...

15:03.536 --> 15:05.504
...he didn't try in the first place!

15:18.751 --> 15:19.877
That's enough!

15:29.161 --> 15:31.561
The Shinsengumi will take it from here.

15:33.399 --> 15:35.731
So it was Ito after all...

15:36.368 --> 15:38.427
...who killed Sakamoto?

15:39.572 --> 15:40.903
No.

15:42.908 --> 15:44.500
It was me.

15:50.549 --> 15:53.109
Deputy, what did he mean by that?

15:53.319 --> 15:59.280
It was his fault for not being able
to protect him, that's what he meant.

16:02.261 --> 16:04.252
A time of great change...

16:04.496 --> 16:08.489
Until his death at 33, Ryoma
Sakamoto soared like a dragon...

16:08.634 --> 16:11.728
...throughout this turbulent era.

16:12.137 --> 16:15.106
Over the years, many
theories were advanced as to...

16:15.241 --> 16:17.766
...who was behind his assassination.

16:18.344 --> 16:23.281
But to this day, the truth
remains buried in history.

16:23.682 --> 16:26.708
Mutsu disappeared without
ever telling what he knew...

16:26.819 --> 16:30.915
...and the Shinsengumi never asked.

16:31.790 --> 16:34.623
Ito's group was massacred
here at Aburanokoji...

16:34.727 --> 16:40.393
...by the Shinsengumi, so the story
goes.

17:09.395 --> 17:11.192
Since it's such a nice day today...

17:11.330 --> 17:14.766
...I thought I'd go look at
the cherry blossoms with Izumi.

17:15.067 --> 17:17.228
Could you make us some
lunch to take along?

17:17.469 --> 17:20.666
Miss Sanako's going to join us. Right?

17:20.773 --> 17:25.506
If you want to catch his eye, you
better not let him out of your sight!

17:42.261 --> 17:45.856
Ryoma, don't worry, I'll
see to it that she gets this.

17:52.037 --> 17:55.200
<i>Chiba dojo</i>

17:56.442 --> 17:58.171
Ryoma's dead?

18:00.379 --> 18:01.676
It's not true!

18:07.820 --> 18:10.414
This is for you, Miss Sanako...

18:15.027 --> 18:20.431
Two days before he was killed, he
ripped it off his arm as a memento...

18:20.966 --> 18:22.831
...and asked me to bring it to you.

18:34.713 --> 18:36.112
Ryoma!

18:37.182 --> 18:39.343
You had your whole life ahead of you!

18:40.853 --> 18:42.650
Ryoma...

18:44.623 --> 18:46.352
Don't cry for him...

18:47.159 --> 18:50.287
Ryoma was a dragon incarnation,
sent from Heaven to...

18:50.829 --> 18:53.491
...take control in this turbulent era.

18:54.166 --> 18:55.827
He's not dead.

18:56.035 --> 18:59.198
His job was done, so he went
back to Heaven, that's all!

18:59.371 --> 19:04.638
If that's the case,
then why are you crying?

19:08.147 --> 19:09.341
Because...

19:09.648 --> 19:14.085
It's not Ryoma Sakamoto, the
dragon incarnation sent from Heaven...

19:14.219 --> 19:15.652
...but someone else...

19:16.488 --> 19:20.447
I'm mourning the loss of a
friend who was just too gentle!

19:30.502 --> 19:31.161
Ryoma...

19:32.471 --> 19:33.802
My friend...

19:34.773 --> 19:37.298
You left us too soon, after all!

19:55.928 --> 20:00.456
The thing is, I've always felt
something calling to me, deep inside...

20:02.034 --> 20:04.195
I'd like to have a Kurofune of my own!

20:04.470 --> 20:06.233
I want to get my hands on one...

20:06.405 --> 20:09.568
...and I want to
travel around the world...

20:09.775 --> 20:11.606
that's my dream!

20:14.813 --> 20:16.872
Ryoma, you can have this.

20:19.685 --> 20:20.845
Izumi...

20:21.186 --> 20:23.677
In return, when you do get
your hands on a Kurofune...

20:23.822 --> 20:25.551
...then I want you to send word to me.

20:25.657 --> 20:28.057
Take me with you around the world!

20:35.234 --> 20:36.929
It's a promise.

20:54.353 --> 20:55.752
Ryoma...

20:57.456 --> 21:02.553
I want to get my hands on one and
I want to travel around the world...

21:02.794 --> 21:04.659
That's my dream!

21:11.236 --> 21:15.263
I would've given anything
to see the world with you...

21:15.407 --> 21:16.241
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:16.241 --> 21:18.010
Ryoma!
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:18.010 --> 21:20.444
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:31.089 --> 21:43.126
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:43.402 --> 21:53.141
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:53.278 --> 22:02.277
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:02.421 --> 22:13.093
<i>Even if it's just "hello"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:14.132 --> 22:20.264
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

22:20.639 --> 22:23.631
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:24.509 --> 22:30.778
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:31.083 --> 22:36.578
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:51.837 --> 22:53.532
A new era is upon us...

22:54.106 --> 22:58.475
But there's a promise I made that
I have to keep no matter what.

22:59.645 --> 23:01.579
Next episode of Age of Chaos...

23:01.747 --> 23:03.112
The Promise

23:03.282 --> 23:05.910
Pay close attention, and wait!
